    <string name="gm_intro">A game mode is a set of real system settings applied when a game opens and undone when it ends. A game\'s own profile can override brightness and Do Not Disturb.</string>
    <string name="gm_active_title">Running now</string>
    <string name="gm_default_title">Default mode</string>
    <string name="gm_default_desc">Used for games that do not choose a mode in their own profile.</string>
    <string name="gm_edit_title">What each mode changes</string>
    <string name="gm_change_brightness">Set brightness</string>
    <string name="gm_change_brightness_desc">Needs Modify system settings access. Your own brightness is put back afterwards.</string>
    <string name="gm_dnd">Do Not Disturb</string>
    <string name="gm_dnd_desc">Silences notifications except what Android lets through as priority. Needs Do Not Disturb access.</string>
    <string name="gm_keep_awake">Keep the screen awake</string>
    <string name="gm_keep_awake_desc">Stops the screen from turning off on its own while a game is open and the assistant is running.</string>
    <string name="gm_change_volume">Set media volume</string>
    <string name="gm_change_volume_desc">Your own volume is put back afterwards.</string>
    <string name="gm_interval">The panel refreshes every %1$d s in this mode.</string>
    <string name="gm_reset">Reset this mode</string>
    <string name="gm_access_title">Access these settings need</string>
    <string name="gm_limits_title">What a mode cannot do</string>
    <string name="gm_limits_body">Android does not let ordinary apps change CPU or GPU speed, so no mode claims to boost performance that way. Modes only remove interruptions and manage brightness, volume and screen timeout. Changes are applied while the assistant is running; if it is stopped, nothing is applied.</string>
    <string name="tb_intro">Real controls for your phone. Each one changes an actual system setting or opens the system page for it.</string>
